    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d438">

                <pb facs="0423" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/8069: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Ecuador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-04T23:00:00-04:00">August 4, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>562. Your 626, July 31 and 632, August 1.<anchor n="92" xml:id="d438-f1"/> Rubber
                    Reserve has instructed Grace and Company to purchase rubber at agreement price
                    pending conclusion of arrangements with Ecuadorian Development Corporation.
                    Reports received from Grace and Company indicate rubber destined for Argentina
                    referred to in your no. 587 of July 18<anchor n="93" xml:id="d438-f2"/> has been
                    acquired for Rubber Reserve. Please confirm.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
